#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Post-generation wrapper for the OpenRouter/Nemotron lane (Dialectica).

MEKANISME §34. The raw Nemotron 3 Ultra output measured in the OpenRouter
benchmark (BENCH-2026-11-10) has three consistent, mechanical defects:

1. Mojibake: the answer arrives double-encoded (UTF-8 bytes read as
   Latin-1), 31-88+ markers per answer ("EIPâ€'1167", "Ã—").
2. Length: median 3,846 chars against the rubric floor of 4,500 (§30 R3).
3. Citation binding (experiment E1 in QUALITY.md): numbers are repeatedly
   attached to the WRONG named document (EIP-2929 given the pre-Berlin
   700-gas CALL cost; EIP-3860 credited with a DELEGATECALL surcharge;
   EIP-1167 given a 10-byte bytecode). Rubric item (d) is a dead gate:
   a draft that fails it is never sent.

This module is the mechanical fence. It never invents a source and never
calls a model itself; regeneration is injected by the caller as a
callback. Pipeline: normalise mojibake -> length guard (one regeneration
with an explicit expansion instruction when below the floor; still short
= GAGAL-LANJUT, do not send) -> number/citation audit + citation_patch
(wrong or unverifiably-bound numbers are REMOVED, never replaced with an
invented value) -> automatic QUALITY.md rubric score (a)-(g).

Canonical values used by the audit are the values written in the named
documents themselves, cross-checked against the steering ground truth for
ISR 60fa9935 and the BENCH spot-audit: EIP-1167 runtime bytecode = 45
bytes; EIP-2929 cold account access = 2,600 gas, warm = 100 gas (700 gas
is the pre-Berlin CALL base cost, not EIP-2929); EIP-3860 = initcode
metering, limit 49,152 bytes and 2 gas per 32-byte word (it is NOT a
DELEGATECALL or CALL surcharge); EIP-2028 = 16 gas per non-zero calldata
byte, 4 gas per zero byte; EIP-170 max contract size = 24,576 bytes.

MEKANISME §45 (post-falsified-#2 gate): the audit above only judges
numbers bound to named documents, so a draft with almost NO citations
and almost NO numbers gives it nothing to judge — claim #2 (ISO
097df475) shipped with 0 URLs and passed. The mechanical floor below
(K-1/K-2 from STUDI-JUARA-VERDICT-2026-11-10, n=153 verified / 204
falsified external) is the complementary dead gate: a draft is NOT
sendable when it has < 1 URL, citation density < 0.5 per 1,000 chars,
or a citation-bound number ratio < 0.30. Floor failures are reported as
findings (severity FLOOR, span None) so every lane's existing fail-
closed sendable semantics (any surviving finding = withheld) applies
without any provider change; the semantic support gate (self-VFP,
operator prompt T10.2/T12) remains a separate, non-delegable check —
claim #1 passed every mechanical threshold and died on support.
"""

